  "final_response": "Done. The change is in `src/main.c:355-373`.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`src/main.c`** — the two identical positional-argument bodies (one for `args_done`, one for `!isoptish`) are merged into one branch, with `program` capture folded in as the first case:\n\n```c\nif (args_done || !isoptish(argv[i])) {\n  if (!program) {\n    program = argv[i];\n  } else if (further_args_are_strings) {\n    ...\n} else if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"--\")) {\n  args_done = 1;\n} else {\n  /* options */\n```\n\nThe `if (!program) usage(2, 1);` guard on `--` is gone, so the filter can now be a positional argument after `--`. Net effect on behavior:\n\n- `jq -- '.'`, `jq --args -- '$ARGS.positional' foo` now work instead of printing a usage error.\n- `jq --` with nothing after it no longer errors immediately; `program` stays unset and falls through to the existing tail logic (`.` when not a tty, otherwise `usage(2, 1)`) — the same as bare `jq`.\n- Everything already accepted keeps working: options before/after the filter, `--` before input files, `-f -- prog.jq`.\n\n**`tests/shtest`** — three cases added next to the existing `--args`/`--jsonargs` tests: filter after `--`; filter after `--` with following positional strings that look like options (`-n`, `--args`); and a literal `--` consumed as a positional string.\n\n**Docs** — the `--` entry in `docs/content/manual/manual.yml` now says the first remaining argument is taken as the filter if not yet given, with the matching line updated in `jq.1.prebuilt` (this repo commits regenerated manpages alongside manual.yml edits).\n\n## Verification — incomplete\n\nI could not run the test suite. There are no autotools in this environment (`autoreconf`/`automake` are absent), so I set up a manual compile instead; that got as far as compiling `src/main.c` cleanly with `-Wall -Wextra`, but executing any locally built binary (the generator for `src/builtin.inc`, and hence a built `jq`) required approval that wasn't granted, so the three new `shtest` cases are unrun. They're reasoned through against the new control flow, not observed passing. Scratch files from the attempt were removed; the working tree contains only the four changes above."
